= Citation — Technical =

Structured citations can be represented as typed relationships between persistent identifiers and bibliographic metadata. Citation graphs support discovery and analysis, but their edges are semantically heterogeneous: a work may cite another to support, extend, contrast, criticize, reuse data from, or simply contextualize it.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* citation ≠ endorsement
* citation count ≠ quality
* citation ≠ evidence of correctness

